text:
Restrain, my child,
the surge of a mind too little sound, and tame the flames;
curb your grief, show yourself the wife of Hercules.

A worse fortune inflames love the more:
he loves even this very thing, that she lacks her father's home,
that her hair lies bare of gold and gem;
in his pity perhaps he loves her very sufferings;
this is habitual with Hercules: he loves captives.

Restrain, father, the dire threats of your wraths;
she has it, it is done, the punishment you seek she has paid:
slain by her own right hand, your mother lies.
